<p>If your printer is equipped with the perfect binder, the Perfect Binding 
 function is available. Perfect binding is a binding method that applies 
 heated glue to printed sheets to form a book block, encloses the book 
 block in a cover sheet, and trims away excess paper to create neat edges.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about perfect binding and supported 
 paper types and sizes, see the operating instructions provided with the 
 printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>On the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 tab, specify the size of original and the paper source tray.<br/>
 You can also specify them on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> 
 and <span class="Term-Soft">Paper</span> menus of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed 
 Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Finishing</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding</span> 
 check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span>.<br/>The <a href="~/Topics/idh_dperfect_binding"><span class="Term-Soft">Perfect 
 Binding Details</span></a> dialog box appears.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Binding Position:</span> 
 list, select a binding position.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Binding Paper Source 
 Tray:</span> list, select a paper source tray for the cover sheet.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Cutting 
 Options:</span> list, select a cut method for the cover sheet.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Position</span> 
 area, you can specify a distance by which you want to shift the print 
 image on the book block pages.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Cut Position</span> 
 area, specify the necessary settings according to the cutting method selected 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Cutting Options:</span> list. 
 The shaded settings are unavailable.<br/>For details about Perfect Binding cutting options, see 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Details</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="11">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Details</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
